">4.84</td><td align="center">1.75</td><td align="center">7.14</td><td align="center">0.41</td><td align="center">3.75</td><td align="center">2.29</td><td align="center">0.62</td><td align="center">0.45</td><td align="center">7.35</td><td align="center">1.67</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p><sup>a </sup>All analyses, except for parent-of-origin, were based on affected relative pairs (ARP). Parent-of-origin was an affected sibling pair (ASP) analysis.</p><p><sup>b </sup>The LOD scores marked in <bold>bold </bold>indicate the analyses that showed an increase in maximum LOD score from the baseline univariate to the covariate LOD that reached genome-wide significance. Chromosome 10, subclinical phenotype c/d/g was genome-wide significant at <italic>p </italic>= 0.063 and has also been indicated in <bold>bold.</bold></p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec></back></article>